{"name":"Kombucha","hex":"#d89f66","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"kombucha","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fermented, effervescent, and sweetened black tea of Mongolian origin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kombucha"}],"entries":[{"title":"Kombucha","blocks":[{"text":"Kombucha is a fermented, effervescent and sweetened black tea drink. Sometimes the beverage is called kombucha tea to distinguish it from the culture of bacteria and yeast. Juice, spices, fruit, or other flavorings are often added. Commercial kombucha contains small amounts of alcohol."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Kombucha_Mature.jpg/330px-Kombucha_Mature.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kombucha","wikidata":"Q657032"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Kombuchacultsm.jpg/330px-Kombuchacultsm.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Kombuchacultsm.jpg/330px-Kombuchacultsm.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Yeast and bacteria in kombucha magnified 400 times","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKombuchacultsm.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/SCOBY_mushroom.jpg/500px-SCOBY_mushroom.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/SCOBY_mushroom.jpg/1280px-SCOBY_mushroom.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/SCOBY_mushroom.jpg/500px-SCOBY_mushroom.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A SCOBY used for brewing kombucha","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3